WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.790
A share car's return checklist is often the only inspection it gets between bookings.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.600
A new paper asks which items renters really check,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.080
and which they tick from memory.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.430
We didn't ask the renters.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.310
We worked from the app's own log:

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.810
how long each answer took, and whether a photo went with it.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.380
Across one thousand eight hundred and forty-two returns,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.530
each answer was classed as a measured check, a visual check, a memory tick or a skip.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.380
A memory tick means not looking at the car again.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.330
Sixty-one per cent of the time, the fuel was checked against the gauge.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.640
Seventy-one per cent of the time, the toll transponder was ticked from memory.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.450
A fuel shortfall costs you at the next refuelling stop.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.490
A missing transponder turns up, if at all, on a later invoice.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.170
You may never connect the two.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.320
The closer the late-return fee, the more gets ticked from memory:

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.890
twenty-two per cent with over fifteen minutes to go,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.810
fifty-eight in the final five.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.490
Through it all, the completion rate held above ninety-seven per cent.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:09.070
Midway through the study, the operator made the transponder field require a photo.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.850
With time to spare, it worked.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.630
Memory ticks on that field fell from sixty-eight per cent to forty-one.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.820
But in the final five minutes, seventy-four only became seventy-one.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.330
The step still gets performed.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.850
What changes is whether anyone’s looking at what the photo shows.
